I dive on the Kwinana Grain Terminal for the first time. It is always daunting diving in a new area by yourself. I used an app called VisPro Dive to help me learn about the dive site and forecast conditions before getting in the water, which proved very useful and helped settle my nerves. I get surrounded by Toadfish and see a male and female Shaw's Cowfish. I was pleasantly surprised by the visibility down under this jetty and would definitely be interested in going again. I really want to see a seahorse here, and I know if I had dived a little slower and looked a bit harder, I could have found some. Next time!

## Dive stats

- **Location:** Kwinana Grain Terminal, WA
- **Date:** 22 August 2026
- **Depth:** 3.5m avg, 5.3m max
- **Visibility:** 8-12m

## Highlights

Male and Female Shaw's Cowfish, Toadfish, Sea Anemone, and Western Smooth Cowfish
